From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: explorer: Sort, View and Refresh glyphs drawn cleanly

David: the Sort button's up and down arrows and the View icon "look hand
drawn", and Refresh's "arrow points to the tail". Segoe MDL2 Assets is not
installed, so every toolbar glyph is drawn: Sort drew each arrowhead as two
lines with round caps (knobs where they met) -- now one stroke with square
ends, as Up; View's 5-wide squares 2 apart ran together under the 1.25 pen
-- now 4.5-wide one-pixel outlines with a clear gap (the status bar's Large
icons button shares it); Refresh's head sat at the arc's start pointing back
at its tail -- the arc now turns clockwise to the top, where the head points
on round.

